  "__triggerDomains_refinement_note": "P1-1B.1: added 'no_external_trigger' (10 pilot records: low/minimal trigger + neutral affect = spontaneous sharing, no event) and 'indeterminate' (14 records: intensity unknown or context missing in a SINGLE-SIDED corpus — the partner turn that would reveal a trigger is absent). Both cleared the >=3-record admission bar. These SPLIT the former 50% 'other' bucket honestly rather than inventing external-event categories — the directive's event candidates (partner_unavailability, humiliation, loss_of_control) already existed AND were already dead at n=50. Boundaries: no_external_trigger = there IS enough context and there is NO trigger; indeterminate = we CANNOT tell because context is missing; other = residual that fits neither. 'diffuse_internal_state' (1 record) stayed candidate-only, below threshold.",

