  "__maskStrategy_note": "P1-1B.1 (Refinement 3). maskStrategy names HOW a mask is executed, but it is ONLY populated when mask=true, and mask=true requires the FUNCTIONAL test: an action that reduces the direct visibility / accountability / exposure-risk of a vulnerability that was just (or is being) revealed. Consequences of this definition: denial/retract/humor/aggression/command are mask strategies ONLY when they serve vulnerability-reduction — a joke that is just play is NOT a mask, aggression that is just an attack is NOT a mask, a retract that abandons a non-vulnerable claim is NOT a mask. Mask != Repair (repair fixes a damaged bond; mask hides an over-exposed need), Mask != Future_bind (only both when future projection also lowers current exposure), Mask != Performance (only both when restoring persona also reduces vulnerability visibility), Mask != Teasing (teasing can be play/provocation/affection/mask — decide by function). See TRANSITION_GUIDE / ANNOTATION_GUIDE_REVISED §mask.",

